# cluster.example — copy to input/cluster and name the doors.
#
# One line per door:
#   name host port kind
#
# The format matches the porch in gif-generator and the doors in
# backwards-reader on purpose. A door is an address that answers; what stands
# behind it — one machine, three little minds, a split model — is not this
# program's business.
#
# kind is one of:
#   completion   answers /completion
#   embedding    answers /embedding
#   both         answers both, because one llama-server can
#
# A door with no kind is assumed to be "both".
#
# The interpreter will refuse to start if a named door does not answer. It will
# not quietly fall back to running everything here — a cluster you thought was
# helping and wasn't is worse than no cluster, because the timings lie. If you
# want to play on this machine alone, say so out loud:
#
#   here 127.0.0.1 8080 both
#
# Three doors and three roles is the shape this was designed around: while the
# herald writes a scene, the remembrancer can already be searching the
# chronicle, because the search does not depend on the prose. Roles are
# assigned at the start of a session and can move; a door may hold two. A role
# with no door is a stopped program, not a slower one.
#
# cluster-one   192.168.1.41  8080  both
# cluster-two   192.168.1.42  8080  both
# cluster-three 192.168.1.43  8080  both
# workstation   192.168.0.115 8080  completion
# local-gpu     127.0.0.1     8080  both
